<title>NETHERLANDS: Stork H1 net profit rises 22 percent.</title>
<headline>Stork H1 net profit rises 22 percent.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half of 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     1.35 vs   1.13</p>
<p>    Net profit			    40.4  vs  33.2</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		  1.41 vs   1.53</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    54.9  vs  50.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts expected industrial systems and services group Stork NV to post a first-half net profit of between 36 million and 47 million guilders.  </p>
<p>    Net interest		 credit  5.1  vs   3.9  debit</p>
<p>    Tax				     14.7  vs  18.2</p>
<p>    Minority interests	  debit  0.8  vs   1.5  credit</p>
<p>    Income from associates    debit  4.1  vs   3.2  credit</p>
<p>NOTES - Stork's first-half results refer to the first 24 weeks of the year.</p>
<p>Stork said recently acquired aircraft maintenance firm Fokker Aviation was not included in the first-half results but would be included in full-year 1996 results and would make a contribution to full-year profits.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
